  <h1>Java Inheritance</h1>

  <p>Inheritance is one of the core features of object-oriented programming. It allows a class (child) to inherit fields and methods from another class (parent).</p>

  <p><strong>Benefits of Inheritance:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Code reusability</li>
    <li>Improved organization and structure</li>
    <li>Supports hierarchical classifications</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Simple Java Code:</strong></p>
  <pre><code>
class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes a sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Dog d = new Dog();
        d.sound();
        d.bark();
    }
}
  </code></pre>

